  "explanation": "The question asks specifically for the start of construction of the 'Time-Life Building'. Source D1S2 explicitly states: 'Construction on the Time-Life Building's steelwork started in April 1958'. This matches the entity and the action 'construction started'. The alternative candidate 'June 1936' (from D2S2) refers to the excavation of a 'new building at 1 Rockefeller Plaza' (later identified as 9 Rockefeller Plaza), which is a different project or phase described in a different context (Document 2). While Document 2 mentions blueprints were retained for the Time & Life Building, it does not state that the 1936 excavation was the start of the Time-Life Building's construction itself. The audit label J_A/J_B correctly identifies C1 ('June 1936') as a 'wrong_argument' because it refers to a different event (excavation of a different building/phase) rather than the specific construction start of the Time-Life Building. Therefore, only 'April 1958' is the correct answer."
}
